  description: Barhi dates are special because you can eat them yellow and crunchy,
    or brown and soft.
  origin: Originally from Iraq; now grown in many Gulf countries
  appearance: Yellow when fresh, turning brown when ripe
  texture: Crunchy when yellow, soft when brown
  taste: Sweet like honey and caramel
  funFact: 'Barhi can be eaten at two stages: crunchy and yellow, or soft and brown!'
  benefits:
  - Natural energy boost
  - Contains fibre
  nutritionNote: Like most dates, it has natural sugars for energy, plus fibre and
    minerals such as potassium.
  quizFeedback: Barhi dates are yellow and crunchy when fresh, and soft and brown
    when ripe.
